\set ECHO none
--- part 1: adopting another role's table is refused
refused 42501: must be owner of table victim
victim owner: hsv_victim, rls: false, acl: default
registered as history: 0
mine has system versioning: 0
native: refused 42501: must be owner of table victim
--- part 2: adopting one's own table, and a table of an inherited role, works

mine_history owner: hsv_evil

grp_history owner: hsv_member
native: refused 42501: must be owner of table mine_history
--- part 3: no CREATE on the schema
add_system_versioning: refused 42501: permission denied for schema hsv
native CREATE TABLE: refused 42501: permission denied for schema hsv
t
nc_pk
add_for_portion_of_view: refused 42501: permission denied for schema hsv
add_current_view: refused 42501: permission denied for schema hsv
native CREATE VIEW: refused 42501: permission denied for schema hsv
with CREATE, add_system_versioning: allowed
with CREATE, add_for_portion_of_view: allowed
with CREATE, add_current_view: allowed
--- part 4: a history table another role owns is neither dropped nor re-owned
rebuild_system_versioning_views: allowed
drop_system_versioning: refused 42501: must be owner of table mine_history
native DROP TABLE: refused 42501: must be owner of table mine_history
mine_history owner: hsv_victim
owner again, rebuild_system_versioning_views: allowed
owner again, drop_system_versioning: allowed
schema owner, drop_system_versioning: allowed
schema owner, native DROP TABLE of another role's table: allowed
